  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "This was originally requested and closed due to age at https://vrchat.canny.io/feature-requests/p/give-portals-the-ability-to-set-a-destination-spawn-location -- I have reopened it as per the request of Tupper on the post.\n\nThe idea is largely the same, but for the sake of explanation:\n\nThe purpose of this feature is to allow world portals to access specific designated spawn points in first or third party worlds. The primary target of this is world portals, whether or not player placed portals can do this is irrelevant to me personally.\n\nThis could be used to achieve more immersive world linking, especially in scenarios where a large collection of interlinked worlds, especially between organized third parties, would benefit from this. \n\nIf I make a world with a fancy intergalactic train station, I might talk to my friend John Doe and say \"Hey, you have this train station in your world, can you add a named spawn point there that I can target?\" - then, when people use a portal I put in my train, they will be sent to John Doe's world and spawn at the station, instead of at the world's normal spawn location.",
